  "body": "GraalVM is an advanced JDK with ahead-of-time Native Image compilation. You can use GraalVM just like any other Java Development Kit in your IDE.\r\n\r\nThe project website at https://www.graalvm.org/ describes how to [get started](https://www.graalvm.org/jdk25.3/docs/getting-started/). The release notes can be found on the website: https://www.graalvm.org/release-notes/25.3/.\r\n\r\nAdditional language runtimes such as [Python](https://github.com/oracle/graalpython/releases/tag/graal-25.3.4.1), [JavaScript and Node.js](https://github.com/oracle/graaljs/releases/tag/graal-25.3.4.1), designed for use with GraalVM 25.3.4.1, are available for download as standalone distributions in the related repositories.\r\n\r\nHere are the convenience links for the JDK base downloads of GraalVM:\r\n\r\n| Platform        | Graal 25i3 / JDK25                                                                                                                                                  | Instructions                                                                  |\r\n| --------------- | :-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------: | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\r\n| Linux (amd64)   | [:arrow_down: download](https://github.com/graalvm/graalvm-ce-builds/releases/download/graal-25.3.4.1/graalvm-community-jdk-25i3-25.0.4.1_linux-x64_bin.tar.gz)     | [*instructions*](https://www.graalvm.org/jdk25.3/docs/getting-started/linux/)   |\r\n| Linux (aarch64) | [:arrow_down: download](https://github.com/graalvm/graalvm-ce-builds/releases/download/graal-25.3.4.1/graalvm-community-jdk-25i3-25.0.4.1_linux-aarch64_bin.tar.gz) | [*instructions*](https://www.graalvm.org/jdk25.3/docs/getting-started/linux/)   |\r\n| macOS (aarch64) | [:arrow_down: download](https://github.com/graalvm/graalvm-ce-builds/releases/download/graal-25.3.4.1/graalvm-community-jdk-25i3-25.0.4.1_macos-aarch64_bin.tar.gz) | [*instructions*](https://www.graalvm.org/jdk25.3/docs/getting-started/macos/)   |\r\n| Windows (amd64) | [:arrow_down: download](https://github.com/graalvm/graalvm-ce-builds/releases/download/graal-25.3.4.1/graalvm-community-jdk-25i3-25.0.4.1_windows-x64_bin.zip)      | [*instructions*](https://www.graalvm.org/jdk25.3/docs/getting-started/windows/) |\r\n\r\nBased on the commit: [https://github.com/oracle/graal/tree/graal-25.3.4.1](https://github.com/oracle/graal/tree/graal-25.3.4.1).\r\n\r\n### Container Images\r\n\r\nGraalVM Community container images for this version are available in the [GitHub Container Registry](https://github.com/orgs/graalvm/packages). \r\n\r\nTo pull GraalVM JDK with Docker:\r\n```\r\n$ docker pull ghcr.io/graalvm/jdk-community:25i3-25.0.4.1\r\n```\r\nTo use GraalVM JDK as a base image in a Dockerfile:\r\n```\r\nFROM ghcr.io/graalvm/jdk-community:25i3-25.0.4.1\r\n```\r\n",
